<title>BELGIUM: EU sees lower 1997/98 beet sugar output.</title>
<headline>EU sees lower 1997/98 beet sugar output.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union beet sugar output is expected to fall to 16.05 million tonnes in 1997/98 (July/June) from 16.51 million last season, the European Commission said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>It also saw 1.0 million tonnes of non-quota &quot;C&quot; sugar being carried over into 1998/99, against 917,000 tonnes carried over into 1997/98. It put &quot;C&quot; sugar exports at 1.95 million tonnes in 1997/98, down from 2.44 million in 1996/97.  </p>
<p>The production forecast, the EU's first for 1997/98, was presented at the weekly meeting of the EU sugar management committee.</p>
<p>The EU sugar beet area was seen 1.1 percent higher at 2.04 million hectares in 1997/98.</p>
<p>But the average white sugar yield was seen falling to 7.86 tonnes per hectare from 8.18 tonnes last season, following drought stress earlier this year.</p>
<p>--Peter Blackburn, Brussels newsroom +322 287 6830</p>
